> Retain the original stricter twelve-update diagnostic

The legacy report also used a separate cubic diagnostic with tolerance1e−14 and
cap12. That control is retained below through the same canonical trace API. Its
residuals now belong to a real native call rather than a second hand-coded root
algorithm. The plotted log10 value is floored at1e−16 only for display; actual
residuals remain in the table. A zero or tiny plotted value is not an exact-root
certificate or an empirical proof of the asymptotic order.

Every actual applied update triggers one new callback. The first three seed
callbacks are always made, including when the update cap is zero. An explicit
final cap check reuses the already evaluated last value and does not fabricate
another callback or parabola.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/muller_strict.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::muller_trace([](double x) {
        return x * x * x - x - 2;
    }, 1, 1.5, 2, 1e-14, 12);
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| actual inspection | legacy iteration label | at cap | actual current x | actual abs " "residual | updated |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &s = t.steps[i];
        x.push_back(i);
        y.push_back(std::log10(std::max(std::abs(s.f[2]), 1e-16)));
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, s.legacy_iteration,
                   s.at_limit, s.x[2], std::abs(s.f[2]), s.updated);
    }
    std::print("\nActual stop: {}. Capture units: {}.\n",
               dm::algorithms::muller_stop_name(t.run.stop), t.captured_entries);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "native stricter run", {124, 58, 237}, 6).title(
        "Original12-update diagnostic: actual stricter residuals").x_label(
        "actual inspection index").y_label("log10 max(abs residual,1e-16)").save_svg("build/muller_strict.svg");
}
```
